{"episodes":{"184857":"An isolated large hail producing storm moved across the James valley during the early morning hours of Friday, September 29th. Ping pong sized hail was observed at a residence 1 mile west of Groton.","185001":"In the morning hours of September 29th, storms dropping hail stones around golf ball-sized moved through west central Minnesota.","185264":"Heavy rainfall was focused in an area near the New York City Metropolitan area on September 29th, 2023. A bulk of the widespread flash flooding was in New York but was close enough to result in localized flash flooding in New Jersey. Rainfall totals in New Jersey were 1-2.5 inches, mainly near the NYC metro.","185266":"An inverted trough extending from a low pressure system over the Western Atlantic provided a focus for persistent heavy convective rain to continually develop over the NYC metro and surrounding areas during much of the day on September 29th, 2023. In an environment with anomalously high moisture given the time of year, PWATs near 1.5-1.7 inches, rounds of heavy rainfall fell over the same areas for more than 12-18 hours. While the rainfall rates were generally 1 inch per hour or less, the persistence in the heavier rainfall resulted in a widespread total of 4-6 inches of rain with JFK receiving almost 9 inches of rain from the event. There were some brief periods of time where rainfall rates peaked at near 2 inches per hour. This resulted in widespread flash flooding across Southeast NY and Southern Connecticut.","185267":"An inverted trough extending from a low pressure system over the Western Atlantic provided a focus for persistent heavy convective rain to continually develop over the NYC metro and surrounding areas during much of the day on September 29th, 2023. In an environment with anomalously high moisture given the time of year, PWATs near 1.5-1.7 inches, rounds of heavy rainfall fell over the same areas for more than 12-18 hours. While the rainfall rates were generally 1 inch per hour or less, the persistence in the heavier rainfall resulted in a widespread total of 4-6 inches of rain with JFK receiving almost 9 inches of rain from the event. There were some brief periods of time where rainfall rates peaked at near 2 inches per hour. This resulted in widespread flash flooding across Southeast NY and Southern Connecticut.","185895":"Scattered thunderstorms developed along a frontal boundary during the mid to late afternoon as convergence moved from far eastern South Dakota into southwest Minnesota. A decent amount of mid-level instability resulted in MLCAPE up to 1500 J/kg while deep-layer shear remained largely less than 30 kts. This environment favored storms that produced large hail.","185896":"Scattered thunderstorms developed along a frontal boundary during the mid to late afternoon as convergence moved from far eastern South Dakota into southwest Minnesota. A decent amount of mid-level instability resulted in MLCAPE up to 1500 J/kg while deep-layer shear remained largely less than 30 kts. This environment favored storms that produced large hail.","186065":"The month of September concluded with thunderstorms that brought heavy rain, rockslides, high elevation mountain snow, and a funnel cloud report.","186114":"A dissipating front across Central Florida along with a wide area of moisture streaming northward across the region led to the formation of locally heavy showers and thunderstorms during the afternoon hours across SE Florida.","186147":"A cold front brought active weather into parts of northern California and western Nevada mostly north of US-50 during this period. A 15-20% chance for isolated thunderstorms A narrow band of showers along a cold front passage overnight Friday into Saturday morning was followed by a 15-20% chance for isolated thunderstorms Saturday afternoon. Then intermittent bands of valley rain/mountain snow showers followed later Saturday night through early Sunday morning.","186323":"Heavy rain from thunderstorms resulted in flooding across parts of Litchfield County in northwestern Connecticut on September 29, 2023."},"events":[{"begin":"2023-09-29T11:49Z","county":"Brown","damageCrops":"0.00K","damageProperty":"0.00K","deaths":0,"end":"2023-09-29T11:49Z","endLat":45.33,"endLon":-98.3,"episode":184857,"id":1131776,"injuries":0,"lat":45.33,"location":"1.19 NE Stratford","lon":-98.3,"magnitude":1.0,"source":"Trained Spotter","state":"SD","type":"Hail","wfo":"ABR"},{"begin":"2023-09-29T11:56Z","county":"Brown","damageCrops":"0.00K","damageProperty":"0.00K","deaths":0,"end":"2023-09-29T11:56Z","endLat":45.46,"endLon":-98.12,"episode":184857,"id":1131777,"injuries":0,"lat":45.46,"location":"1.19 NW Groton","lon":-98.12,"magnitude":1.5,"source":"Public","state":"SD","type":"Hail","wfo":"ABR"},{"begin":"2023-09-29T12:30Z","county":"Kings","damageCrops":"0.00K","damageProperty":"0.00K","deaths":0,"end":"2023-09-29T13:00Z","endLat":40.5846,"endLon":-73.9838,"episode":185266,"id":1135742,"injuries":0,"lat":40.59,"location":"0.87 NW Coney Is","lon":-73.99,"narrative":"Vehicle stranded in flood waters at the intersection of Belt Parkway and Cropsey Avenue. Belt Parkway is closed in both directions.","source":"Public","state":"NY","type":"Flash Flood","wfo":"OKX"},{"begin":"2023-09-29T12:35Z","county":"Kings","damageCrops":"0.00K","damageProperty":"0.00K","deaths":0,"end":"2023-09-29T13:05Z","endLat":40.6018,"endLon":-73.9786,"episode":185266,"id":1135743,"injuries":0,"lat":40.6,"location":"1.38 N Coney Is","lon":-73.98,"narrative":"David A Boody School is flooded and being evacuated.","source":"Public","state":"NY","type":"Flash Flood","wfo":"OKX"},{"begin":"2023-09-29T12:38Z","county":"Kings","damageCrops":"0.00K","damageProperty":"0.00K","deaths":0,"end":"2023-09-29T13:08Z","endLat":40.6488,"endLon":-73.974,"episode":185266,"id":1135745,"injuries":0,"lat":40.65,"location":"2.62 W Brooklyn","lon":-73.98,"narrative":"Car stranded in flood waters at the intersection of Prospect 